module test.claim.self_host_logic_seed_unavailable_witness

import tools.self_host_logic_seed_unavailable_transport {
  slbu_seed_unavailable_receipt_holds
}

// Seed-unavailable self-host behavioral receipt for dag/std/logic.dag (Control (b)):
// tools.self_host_logic_seed_unavailable_transport emits dag/std/logic.dag via the
// real gunbc binary, compiles the emitted Rust WITHOUT the seed crate (pure std
// dependencies only -- self-contained dag module), and runs the resulting witness
// binary to prove seed independence by construction: no seed crate at link time
// means seed linkage is structurally impossible.
//
// THIS IS NOT A SUBSTITUTE FOR CONTROL (a). Control (b) tests whether the candidate
// depends on the seed; control (a) tests whether the comparison discriminates. Neither
// establishes the other, and a green (b) does not cover a missing (a).
//
// CLASSIFIED onto LocalRepoWetLane: the only external effect beyond temp directory
// operations is a cargo build of a zero-external-dependency crate (emitted code uses
// only std), which requires no network access and is structurally the same class as
// the local file and git operations already on that lane. The hermetic envelope
// refuses because shell.Mktemp.Dir, Filesystem.Write, cargo.Build.BuildManifest, and
// gunbc.WitnessBin.Run have no mock_response.

test fn self_host_logic_seed_unavailable_receipt_holds() -> Bool {
  slbu_seed_unavailable_receipt_holds()
}
